NAME
       newusers - create or update many users from a file

SYNOPSIS
       newusers [FILE]

DESCRIPTION
       newusers reads lines in the format of /etc/passwd, with the password
       field holding the clear-text password:

           NAME:PASSWORD:UID:GID:COMMENT:HOME:SHELL

       and creates each user (or updates an existing one). An empty UID or
       GID lets newusers pick one; a GID that is a name creates that group
       when needed. Without FILE it reads standard input. Only root can run
       it. Keep the input file safe and delete it afterwards: it holds
       passwords.

EXAMPLES
           newusers /root/new-accounts.txt

SEE ALSO
       useradd(8), chpasswd(8), passwd(5)
